  "title": "Computational Functionalism",
  "role": "model",
  "summary": "Computational functionalism, from Hilary Putnam's machine state functionalism of 1967 to the AI consciousness report of Butlin, Long, Chalmers and others in 2023: a state is conscious when it plays the right role in the right algorithm, whatever the substrate. So consciousness in AI is possible in principle, and a system can be assessed for it by the computations it performs.",
